0000                             ; =============================================================================
0000                             ;  B8Script interpreter for the Motorola 6809
0000                             ;  Spec: docs/b8script.md (2026-11-21).
0000                             ;  Follows the design of the Z80 interpreter (z80/b8s-z80.asm).
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  Two builds, selected by the CHECKED line below (CPM is always 0: the 6809
0000                             ;  has no CP/M; the line is kept only so that build.sh works):
0000                             ;    CHECKED  0 = no checks (spec: an unchecked build checks nothing)
0000                             ;             1 = a checked build: variables start at 0, words start
0000                             ;                 undefined, and every error in the spec's table stops the
0000                             ;                 program with the four-line report, then goes to EXIT:
0000                             ;                   Err X @ line,col
0000                             ;                   <up to 16 characters of the text at the place>
0000                             ;                   Stk n: ... v v v      (n = depth, then the top 8 values)
0000                             ;                   Rtn n
0000                             ;                 S/s data stack over/underflow, R/r return stack over/
0000                             ;                 underflow, H heap, O store outside the program's space,
0000                             ;                 W bad character after [, U undefined word, Q no closing
0000                             ;                 quote, X reserved byte, Z divide by zero, N unbalanced or
0000                             ;                 mismatched brackets, B Ctrl-C.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  In both builds Ctrl-C stops a running program (the unchecked build goes
0000                             ;  to EXIT without a word): see the console layer below for the rules, the
0000                             ;  held key and the break-off cell at 827Bh.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  Assembler: asm80, M6809 mode.
0000                             ; =============================================================================
0000                CPM:      EQU   0   ; always 0 (no CP/M on the 6809)
0000                CHECKED:   EQU   1   ; 1 = checked build
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                             ;  Register use, everywhere in the interpreter
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;    Y    IP: the address of the next program character to read
0000                             ;    U    the data stack pointer. The stack grows down and U points at the
0000                             ;         top cell (TOS); nothing is cached in a register, because every
0000                             ;         dispatch needs A, B and X as scratch. Cells are big-endian here.
0000                             ;         (Only the stacks are big-endian: cells in RAM that the program can
0000                             ;         see - variables, the heap pointer, anything @ and ! reach - are
0000                             ;         little-endian, as the spec says, so @ and ! swap the bytes.)
0000                             ;    S    the return stack. A word call is a plain push of Y. Entries are
0000                             ;         2 bytes, big-endian. Handlers are called with JSR, so the return
0000                             ;         address of the dispatcher is on top of S while a handler runs.
0000                             ;    DP   the letter page, so the letter-page variables below cost 2-byte
0000                             ;         direct addressing. Nothing else may change DP.
0000                             ;    A B X are scratch. Every handler is entered by JSR and ends in RTS (one
0000                             ;    byte). A handler that pushes or pops the return stack first pulls the
0000                             ;    dispatcher's return address into X (PULS X) and ends with JMP ,X.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  Dispatch (unchecked build). PTAB holds one byte per punctuation character:
0000                             ;  the low byte of the handler's distance from PTAB. The handlers of the last
0000                             ;  characters (in code order) start within 256 bytes after PTAB, the handlers
0000                             ;  of the first NPG1 characters in the 256 bytes after that. The assembler
0000                             ;  works NPG1 out from where five handlers landed, and testing/chktab09.py
0000                             ;  checks the layout. The checked build is bigger than that reach, so its
0000                             ;  table holds whole addresses instead.
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                             ;  Memory map. Everything the interpreter writes is in four RAM areas:
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;    8000h-80FFh  return stack (S); empty = 8100h. Unchecked: 127 entries.
0000                             ;                 Checked: 112 entries (S down to 8020h); the 32 bytes below
0000                             ;                 are a guard band for what a handler and an interrupt push
0000                             ;                 on top of a full stack before the check runs.
0000                             ;    8100h-81FFh  data stack (U). Unchecked: 127 cells, empty = 8200h.
0000                             ;                 Checked: 126 cells (U from 81FCh, empty, down to 8100h):
0000                             ;                 the 4 bytes above are a guard band, so a handler that runs
0000                             ;                 on an empty stack writes there and not on the letter
0000                             ;                 cells. A push past the last cell lands on the return
0000                             ;                 stack's bottom entry (80FEh), and the program stops with S
0000                             ;                 before anything reads it.
0000                             ;    8200h-82FFh  letter page (LET): A..Z at +00h..+33h, a..z at +40h..+73h
0000                             ;                 (a word cell is always 64 bytes below its variable), the
0000                             ;                 heap pointer at +7Ch (= z10+), interpreter variables in the
0000                             ;                 gaps, and the -n? line buffer at +80h..+FFh. The break-off
0000                             ;                 cell is at +7Bh (827Bh); +7Ah is free.
0000                             ;    8300h-       PROG, the program text, NUL-terminated; the heap starts
0000                             ;                 after the NUL and grows to HEAPLIM*256 (F000h)
0000                             ;    F000h-       this image (ROM). The reset vector (FFFEh) must point to
0000                             ;                 `start` (see the listing); the image does not contain it.
0000                             ;    FF03h-FF0Bh  the console routines (CONOUT, KEY) and EXIT are supplied
0000                             ;                 by the system and need no space here.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  The stacks sit below the letter page, so "the program's own space" (what
0000                             ;  the checked build lets ! and . write) is the single range LET..HEAPLIM*256.
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                             ; ---- generic machine: edit these to suit -----------------------------------
0000                KEY:      EQU   0FF06h   ; a waiting key in A, or A = 0 if none is
0000                             ;   waiting. The Z flag must match A (end the
0000                             ;   routine with TSTA / RTS, or a plain LDA).
0000                CONOUT:   EQU   0FF03h   ; print the character in A
0000                EXIT:     EQU   0FF09h   ; where to go when the program ends
0000                             ;   Both are called with JSR. They may change A and CC and must preserve
0000                             ;   B, X, Y, U and DP.
0000                RSPAGE:   EQU   80h   
0000                DSPAGE:   EQU   81h   
0000                LETPAGE:   EQU   82h   
0000                PROG:     EQU   8300h   ; where the loader puts the program text
0000                             ; (the checked startup counts on it being
0000                             ; the page after LETPAGE)
0000                HEAPLIM:   EQU   0F0h   ; the heap must stay below F000h (a page)
0000                MSLOOP:   EQU   20   ; n? inner loop count for about 1 ms; tune it
0000                             ; for your clock and your KEY routine
0000                             ; letter-page layout (direct-page offsets inside LETPAGE)
0000                LET:      EQU   LETPAGE*256   
0000                HEAP:     EQU   7Ch   ; z10+, the heap pointer (little-endian)
0000                KEYBUF:   EQU   34h   ; gap after Z: a key held back by the break check
0000                COUNT:    EQU   35h   ; the break check's countdown (1 look in 256)
0000                AT:       EQU   36h   ; checked: the address of the character being
0000                             ;   run (big-endian), the place an error reports
0000                PEND:     EQU   38h   ; checked: the program's end, the first byte
0000                             ;   after its NUL (big-endian): the heap's floor
0000                SSAV:     EQU   3Ah   ; checked: S as each character starts (big-
0000                             ;   endian): the return stack an error reports
0000                BRKOFF:   EQU   7Bh   ; the break-off cell (827Bh, z9+): 0 = the
0000                             ;   break key is on
0000                LINEBUF:   EQU   LET+80h   ; -n? text, ending in CR
0000                RSTOP:    EQU   RSPAGE*256+100h   ; empty return stack
0000                RSLIM:    EQU   RSPAGE*256+20h   ; checked: S may go no lower between characters
0000                RSREP:    EQU   RSTOP-16   ; checked: S while the error report runs
0000                DSTOP:    EQU   DSPAGE*256+100h-4*CHECKED   ; empty data stack (a guard if checked)
0000                DSLIM:    EQU   DSPAGE*256   ; checked: U may go no lower between characters
F000                          .ORG   0F000h   
F000                             ; =============================================================================
F000                             ;  Console layer: the break key. A running program reads the keyboard only
F000                             ;  through pollk and getk, which between them give the break key its rules:
F000                             ;    - Ctrl-C (03h) stops the program;
F000                             ;    - any other key that the break check reads is held in KEYBUF for the
F000                             ;      next "?", and a newer one takes its place;
F000                             ;    - "?" (getk) takes the held key first;
F000                             ;    - a program that has stored a non-zero byte at BRKOFF gets Ctrl-C as a
F000                             ;      key like any other, but two of them within about 250 ms still stop it.
F000                             ;  On a break the unchecked build ends without a word (EXIT); the checked
F000                             ;  one reports B. All three keep B, X, Y and U.
F000                             ; =============================================================================
F000                             ; pollk: the break check, at every word call and every true ")" loop-back.
F000                             ; It looks at the keyboard only once in 256 calls.
F000   0A 35        POLLK:    DEC   <COUNT   
F002   26 38                  BNE   cc9   
F004   BD FF 06               JSR   KEY   
F007   27 33                  BEQ   cc9   ; no key
F009   97 34                  STA   <KEYBUF   ; held for the next "?"
F00B   20 0D                  BRA   ctlc   
F00D                             ; getk: a key for "?", or A = 0 with the zero flag set if there is none.
F00D   96 34        GETK:     LDA   <KEYBUF   ; a held key goes first, and is taken out of
F00F   27 04                  BEQ   gk1   ;   the buffer (it has been through ctlc)
F011   0F 34                  CLR   <KEYBUF   
F013   4D                     TSTA      ; (CLR set Z: A is not 0)
F014   39                     RTS      
F015   BD FF 06     GK1:      JSR   KEY   
F018   27 22                  BEQ   cc9   
F01A                             ; ctlc: a key has been read. If it is Ctrl-C and the break key is on, that
F01A                             ; is the end. If the program has turned it off, wait about 250 ms for one
F01A                             ; more key: a second Ctrl-C is the end too; any other key is held (the
F01A                             ; newest wins), and the Ctrl-C goes on: A = 3, zero flag clear.
F01A   81 03        CTLC:     CMPA   #3   
F01C   26 1E                  BNE   cc9   
F01E   0D 7B                  TST   <BRKOFF   
F020   27 1B                  BEQ   brk   
F022   34 10                  PSHS   X   
F024   8E 13 88               LDX   #250*MSLOOP   
F027   BD FF 06     CC1:      JSR   KEY   
F02A   26 06                  BNE   cc2   
F02C   30 1F                  LEAX   -1,X   
F02E   26 F7                  BNE   cc1   
F030   20 06                  BRA   cc3   
F032   81 03        CC2:      CMPA   #3   
F034   27 07                  BEQ   brk   
F036   97 34                  STA   <KEYBUF   
F038   86 03        CC3:      LDA   #3   
F03A   35 10                  PULS   X   
F03C   39           CC9:      RTS      
F03D                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                    BRK:      EQU   fin   ; the unchecked build stops without a word;
F03D                          ENDIF      
F03D                          IF   CHECKED   
F03D   86 42        BRK:      LDA   #"B"   ;   the checked build reports B. (The report
F03F   7E F3 68               JMP   error   ;   takes S from SSAV, so the depth of the
F042                          ENDIF      ;   calls here doesn't matter.)
F042   7E FF 09     FIN:      JMP   EXIT   ; the program has ended
F045                             ; =============================================================================
F045                             ;  Startup
F045                             ; =============================================================================
F045   10 CE 81 00  START:    LDS   #RSTOP   
F049   CE 81 FC               LDU   #DSTOP   
F04C   86 82                  LDA   #LETPAGE   
F04E   1F 8B                  TFR   A,DP   
F050                          IF   CHECKED   
F050                             ; Zero the whole letter page: every variable starts at 0, every word
F050                             ; cell at 0 (undefined: a call stops with U), and so do the
F050                             ; interpreter's own cells in the gaps (KEYBUF and the rest). A is
F050                             ; still LETPAGE; 256 rounds leave X at the next page, PROG.
F050   5F                     CLRB      
F051   1F 01                  TFR   D,X   
F053   6F 80        SZ:       CLR   ,X+   
F055   5A                     DECB      
F056   26 FB                  BNE   sz   
F058                          ENDIF      
F058                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                              CLR   <KEYBUF   ; no key held
                              CLR   <BRKOFF   ; the break key is on
                              LDX   #PROG   ; the heap starts after the program's NUL
F058                          ENDIF      
F058   A6 80        SC:       LDA   ,X+   
F05A   26 FC                  BNE   sc   
F05C   1F 10                  TFR   X,D   
F05E   D7 7C                  STB   <HEAP   ; (little-endian)
F060   97 7D                  STA   <HEAP+1   
F062                          IF   CHECKED   
F062   9F 38                  STX   <PEND   ; the heap may never go below this
F064                          ENDIF      
F064   10 8E 83 00            LDY   #PROG   
F068                             ; =============================================================================
F068                             ;  The inner loop: read one character and sort it by range.
F068                             ; 
F068                             ;    00h          end of program
F068                             ;    01h-20h, 7Fh       ignored (control, space, DEL)
F068                             ;    80h-FFh      reserved: ignored, or X in the checked build
F068                             ;    30h-39h      digit: read a whole number
F068                             ;    41h-5Ah      A-Z: call the word in that letter's cell
F068                             ;    61h-7Ah      a-z: push the address of that letter's cell
F068                             ;    the rest     punctuation: JSR through PTAB, 32 entries, in code order
F068                             ; =============================================================================
F068                NEXT:        
F068                          IF   CHECKED   
F068                             ; Both stacks are checked once per character, not in every handler:
F068                             ; the pointer minus its limit, taken as unsigned, must be no more
F068                             ; than the stack's size. Below the limit (an overflow) it wraps to
F068                             ; FFxxh, and the compare leaves N set; above the empty point (an
F068                             ; underflow) it is just over the size, and N is clear.
F068   30 C9 7F 00            LEAX   (0-DSLIM)&0FFFFh,U   
F06C   8C 00 FC               CMPX   #DSTOP-DSLIM   
F06F   22 64                  BHI   e_ds   
F071   30 E9 7F E0            LEAX   (0-RSLIM)&0FFFFh,S   
F075   8C 00 E0               CMPX   #RSTOP-RSLIM   
F078   22 64                  BHI   e_rs   
F07A   10 9F 36               STY   <AT   ; the place, should this character fail
F07D   10 DF 3A               STS   <SSAV   ; and the return stack, as it is now
F080                          ENDIF      
F080   A6 A0                  LDA   ,Y+   
F082   27 BE                  BEQ   fin   ; NUL ends the program
F084   80 21                  SUBA   #21h   ; A = c - 21h
F086   25 E0                  BLO   next   ; 01h-20h ignored
F088   81 0F                  CMPA   #0Fh   
F08A   25 24                  BLO   punct   ; 21h-2Fh: PTAB index 0-14
F08C   80 0F                  SUBA   #0Fh   ; A = c - 30h
F08E   81 0A                  CMPA   #0Ah   
F090   25 26                  BLO   digit   ; 30h-39h
F092   81 11                  CMPA   #11h   
F094   25 18                  BLO   p3a   ; 3Ah-40h
F096   80 11                  SUBA   #11h   ; A = c - 41h
F098   81 1A                  CMPA   #1Ah   
F09A   25 28                  BLO   upper   ; 41h-5Ah: A = letter index 0-25
F09C   81 20                  CMPA   #20h   
F09E   25 0C                  BLO   p5b   ; 5Bh-60h
F0A0   81 3A                  CMPA   #3Ah   
F0A2   25 1A                  BLO   lower   ; 61h-7Ah: A = 20h-39h (cell +64 bytes)
F0A4   81 3E                  CMPA   #3Eh   
F0A6                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                              BHS   next   ; 7Fh-FFh: ignored
F0A6                          ENDIF      
F0A6                          IF   CHECKED   
F0A6   27 C0                  BEQ   next   ; 7Fh (DEL): ignored
F0A8   22 44                  BHI   e_resv   ; 80h-FFh: reserved
F0AA                          ENDIF      
F0AA   80 1A                  SUBA   #1Ah   ; 7Bh-7Eh: -1Eh in all, index 28-31
F0AC   80 09        P5B:      SUBA   #9   ; 5Bh-60h: -4 in all, index 22-27
F0AE   8B 05        P3A:      ADDA   #5   ; 3Ah-40h: index 15-21
F0B0                             ; Punctuation: A = the PTAB index.
F0B0   8E F1 22     PUNCT:    LDX   #PTAB   
F0B3                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                                 ; The handler is at PTAB + D, where B is the table byte and A is 1
                                 ; for the first NPG1 characters, 0 for the rest.
                              LDB   A,X   
                              CMPA   #NPG1   ; carry: one of the first NPG1
                              LDA   #0   ; (leaves the carry alone)
                              ROLA      
                              JSR   D,X   ; the handler ends in RTS
F0B3                          ENDIF      
F0B3                          IF   CHECKED   
F0B3   48                     ASLA      ; the table holds whole addresses
F0B4   AD 96                  JSR   [A,X]   
F0B6                          ENDIF      
F0B6   20 B0                  BRA   next   
F0B8                             ; Digits: step back onto the first digit and read the whole number.
F0B8   31 3F        DIGIT:    LEAY   -1,Y   
F0BA   8D 48                  BSR   rdnum   
F0BC   20 AA                  BRA   next   
F0BE                             ; a-z: push the cell's address (the cell is the variable)
F0BE   8D 36        LOWER:    BSR   cellx   
F0C0   36 10                  PSHU   X   
F0C2   20 A4                  BRA   next   
F0C4                             ; A-Z: call the word. The IP (the address after the letter) goes on the
F0C4                             ; return stack, and the IP becomes the address in the letter's cell.
F0C4                             ; Checked: a cell still 0 (high byte 0) was never defined, since every
F0C4                             ; address in the program's space is 8200h or more. The call has not been
F0C4                             ; made yet, so the report shows the stacks as they were.
F0C4   8D 30        UPPER:    BSR   cellx   
F0C6   E6 84                  LDB   ,X   
F0C8   A6 01                  LDA   1,X   
F0CA                          IF   CHECKED   
F0CA   27 25                  BEQ   e_undef   
F0CC                          ENDIF      
F0CC   34 20                  PSHS   Y   
F0CE   1F 02                  TFR   D,Y   
F0D0   BD F0 00               JSR   pollk   ; the break check, at every word call
F0D3   20 93                  BRA   next   
F0D5                             ; =============================================================================
F0D5                             ;  Checked build: the error entries.
F0D5                             ; 
F0D5                             ;  Each entry loads its letter and then hides the next entry inside a 3-byte
F0D5                             ;  CMPX # (the 8Ch), so that a run of them falls through to one place. The
F0D5                             ;  place an error reports is the address in AT, which the inner loop sets to
F0D5                             ;  each character before it runs it; the one error that reports another
F0D5                             ;  place (W, at the character after the [) changes AT before it comes.
F0D5                             ; 
F0D5                             ;  The report counts the return stack from SSAV, which the inner loop sets
F0D5                             ;  to S before each character, so an error may come from any depth of
F0D5                             ;  calls: a handler, chkst under one, or ctlc under "?" or the break check.
F0D5                             ;  (An r sets SSAV to the empty stack.) The inner loop's own entries are
F0D5                             ;  here, where its short branches reach them; those reached from a handler
F0D5                             ;  are after h_cstore, just ahead of the report.
F0D5                             ; =============================================================================
F0D5                          IF   CHECKED   
F0D5                             ; ---- reached from the inner loop -------------------------------------------
F0D5                             ; The stack checks branch here with N set for an overflow (the pointer is
F0D5                             ; below its limit) and clear for an underflow. After an underflow that stack
F0D5                             ; counts as empty.
F0D5   2B 11        E_DS:     BMI   e_S   
F0D7   CE 81 FC               LDU   #DSTOP   ; s
F0DA   86 73                  LDA   #"s"   
F0DC   20 15                  BRA   eall   
F0DE   2B 0B        E_RS:     BMI   e_R   
F0E0   8E 81 00               LDX   #RSTOP   ; r
F0E3   9F 3A                  STX   <SSAV   
F0E5   86 72                  LDA   #"r"   
F0E7   8C                     FCB   8Ch   
F0E8   86 53        E_S:      LDA   #"S"   
F0EA   8C                     FCB   8Ch   
F0EB   86 52        E_R:      LDA   #"R"   
F0ED   8C                     FCB   8Ch   
F0EE   86 58        E_RESV:   LDA   #"X"   ; a reserved byte (80h-FFh) outside a string
F0F0   8C                     FCB   8Ch   
F0F1   86 55        E_UNDEF:   LDA   #"U"   ; a word never defined (its cell is still 0)
F0F3   7E F3 68     EALL:     JMP   error   
F0F6                          ENDIF      
F0F6                             ; cellx: A = letter index (0-25, or 32-57 for lowercase) -> X = cell address
F0F6   48           CELLX:    ASLA      
F0F7   8E 82 00               LDX   #LET   
F0FA   30 86                  LEAX   A,X   
F0FC   39                     RTS      
F0FD                             ; isdig: A = the character at IP minus "0"; the carry is set if it is a digit
F0FD   A6 A4        ISDIG:    LDA   ,Y   
F0FF   80 30                  SUBA   #"0"   
F101   81 0A                  CMPA   #10   
F103   39           AB9:      RTS      
F104                             ; rdnum: read decimal digits at IP and push the value; IP is left on the
F104                             ; first non-digit. Values wrap at 16 bits, as the spec says. The running
F104                             ; value lives in the new top cell: V = V*10 + digit.
F104   4F           RDNUM:    CLRA      
F105   5F                     CLRB      
F106   36 06                  PSHU   D   
F108   8D F3        RD1:      BSR   isdig   
F10A   24 F7                  BHS   ab9   
F10C   31 21                  LEAY   1,Y   
F10E   34 02                  PSHS   A   
F110   EC C4                  LDD   ,U   
F112   58                     ASLB      
F113   49                     ROLA      
F114   58                     ASLB      
F115   49                     ROLA      
F116   E3 C4                  ADDD   ,U   ; 5V
F118   58                     ASLB      
F119   49                     ROLA      ; 10V
F11A   EB E0                  ADDB   ,S+   
F11C   89 00                  ADCA   #0   
F11E   ED C4                  STD   ,U   
F120   20 E6                  BRA   rd1   
F122                             ; hexc: if the character at IP is a hex digit (0-9, A-F, a-f), step over it
F122                             ; and return its value in A with the carry set; otherwise leave the IP and
F122                             ; return with the carry clear.
F122                             ; (In the unchecked build it is here, ahead of the table, to leave room in
F122                             ; the two ranges after it; the checked build has it next to the grave.)
F122                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                    HEXC:     BSR   isdig   
                              BLO   hv1   ; C = 1
                              ANDA   #0DFh   
                              SUBA   #11h   
                              CMPA   #6   
                              BHS   hv9   ; C = 0
                              SUBA   #0F6h   ; + 10, and sets the carry
                    HV1:      LEAY   1,Y   ; (LEAY leaves the carry alone)
                    HV9:      RTS      
F122                          ENDIF      
F122                             ; =============================================================================
F122                             ;  Dispatch table, in code order.
F122                             ; 
F122                             ;  Unchecked build: one byte per character, the low byte of the handler's
F122                             ;  distance from PTAB. NPG1 is how many characters, from the start, have
F122                             ;  handlers more than 255 bytes past PTAB. ] \ [ @ ? sit where the two ranges
F122                             ;  meet (in falling code order for this), and which side each lands on is
F122                             ;  worked out here. (One division to a line: asm80 only rounds down when it
F122                             ;  stores a value.)
F122                             ; 
F122                             ;  Checked build: it has more code than the two ranges hold, so its table
F122                             ;  holds whole addresses and there are no rules about where handlers go.
F122                             ; =============================================================================
F122                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                    PGRET:    EQU   (h_ret-PTAB)/256   ; 0 = first range, 1 = second
                    PGBRK:    EQU   (h_break-PTAB)/256   
                    PGDEF:    EQU   (h_def-PTAB)/256   
                    PGFET:    EQU   (h_fetch-PTAB)/256   
                    PGKEY:    EQU   (h_key-PTAB)/256   
                    NPG1:     EQU   20 + PGKEY + PGFET + PGDEF + PGBRK + PGRET   
F122                          ENDIF      
F122                PTAB:        
F122                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                              FCB   (h_store-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; !
                              FCB   (h_str-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; "
                              FCB   (h_num-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; #
                              FCB   (h_print-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; $
                              FCB   (h_swap-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; %
                              FCB   (h_and-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; &
                              FCB   (h_emit-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; '
                              FCB   (h_open-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; (
                              FCB   (h_close-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; )
                              FCB   (h_mul-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; *
                              FCB   (h_add-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; +
                              FCB   (h_cfetch-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; ,
                              FCB   (h_sub-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; -
                              FCB   (h_cstore-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; .
                              FCB   (h_div-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; /
                              FCB   (h_dup-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; :
                              FCB   (h_drop-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; ;
                              FCB   (h_lt-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; <
                              FCB   (h_eq-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; =
                              FCB   (h_gt-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; >
                              FCB   (h_key-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; ?
                              FCB   (h_fetch-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; @
                              FCB   (h_def-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; [
                              FCB   (h_break-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; \
                              FCB   (h_ret-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; ]
                              FCB   (h_xor-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; ^
                              FCB   (h_alloc-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; _
                              FCB   (h_grave-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; `
                              FCB   (h_tor-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; {
                              FCB   (h_or-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; |
                              FCB   (h_fromr-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; }
                              FCB   (h_not-PTAB) & 0FFh   ; ~
F122                          ENDIF      
F122                          IF   CHECKED   
F122   F3 35                  FDB   h_store   ; !
F124   F2 41                  FDB   h_str   ; "
F126   F4 38                  FDB   h_num   ; #
F128   F3 1C                  FDB   h_print   ; $
F12A   F3 08                  FDB   h_swap   ; %
F12C   F4 5E                  FDB   h_and   ; &
F12E   F3 14                  FDB   h_emit   ; '
F130   F2 B2                  FDB   h_open   ; (
F132   F2 C6                  FDB   h_close   ; )
F134   F2 D2                  FDB   h_mul   ; *
F136   F4 66                  FDB   h_add   ; +
F138   F2 BE                  FDB   h_cfetch   ; ,
F13A   F4 6D                  FDB   h_sub   ; -
F13C   F3 41                  FDB   h_cstore   ; .
F13E   F4 78                  FDB   h_div   ; /
F140   F3 0F                  FDB   h_dup   ; :
F142   F3 19                  FDB   h_drop   ; ;
F144   F2 F0                  FDB   h_lt   ; <
F146   F2 FC                  FDB   h_eq   ; =
F148   F2 EE                  FDB   h_gt   ; >
F14A   F2 64                  FDB   h_key   ; ?
F14C   F2 5E                  FDB   h_fetch   ; @
F14E   F1 F9                  FDB   h_def   ; [
F150   F1 DC                  FDB   h_break   ; \
F152   F1 D8                  FDB   h_ret   ; ]
F154   F1 6A                  FDB   h_xor   ; ^
F156   F1 88                  FDB   h_alloc   ; _
F158   F1 A4                  FDB   h_grave   ; `
F15A   F1 78                  FDB   h_tor   ; {
F15C   F1 62                  FDB   h_or   ; |
F15E   F1 80                  FDB   h_fromr   ; }
F160   F1 73                  FDB   h_not   ; ~
F162                          ENDIF      
F162                PTABEND:      
F162                             ; =============================================================================
F162                             ;  Handlers that must start in the first range (within 255 bytes of PTAB)
F162                             ;  in the unchecked build: ^ _ ` 00bbIHwg ~
F162                             ; =============================================================================
F162   EC C1        H_OR:     LDD   ,U++   
F164   AA C4                  ORA   ,U   
F166   EA 41                  ORB   1,U   
F168   20 06                  BRA   st0   
F16A   EC C1        H_XOR:    LDD   ,U++   
F16C   A8 C4                  EORA   ,U   
F16E   E8 41                  EORB   1,U   
F170   ED C4        ST0:      STD   ,U   
F172   39                     RTS      
F173   63 C4        H_NOT:    COM   ,U   
F175   63 41                  COM   1,U   
F177   39                     RTS      
F178                             ; "{" ( n -- ) R: ( -- n )     The dispatcher's return address comes off the
F178                             ; return stack first (PULS X) and is jumped to at the end.
F178   35 10        H_TOR:    PULS   X   
F17A   37 06                  PULU   D   
F17C   34 06                  PSHS   D   
F17E   6E 84                  JMP   ,X   
F180                             ; "}" ( -- n ) R: ( n -- )
F180   35 10        H_FROMR:   PULS   X   
F182   35 06                  PULS   D   
F184   36 06                  PSHU   D   
F186   6E 84                  JMP   ,X   
F188                             ; "_" ( n -- addr ): the heap pointer moves by n (signed: a 16-bit add);
F188                             ; TOS is the old pointer.
F188                             ; Checked: the new top must be at least the program's end (PEND) and below
F188                             ; the limit page. That also catches an add that wraps: the top is always
F188                             ; 8301h-EFFFh and n is -32768..32767, so a sum that carries past FFFFh
F188                             ; lands below 7000h, and one that borrows can't happen.
F188   D6 7C        H_ALLOC:   LDB   <HEAP   
F18A   96 7D                  LDA   <HEAP+1   
F18C   1F 01                  TFR   D,X   ; the old pointer
F18E   E3 C4                  ADDD   ,U   
F190                          IF   CHECKED   
F190   10 93 38               CMPD   <PEND   
F193   10 25 01 C9            LBLO   e_heap   ; below the program's end
F197   81 F0                  CMPA   #HEAPLIM   
F199   10 24 01 C3            LBHS   e_heap   ; the new top must stay below the limit page
F19D                          ENDIF      
F19D   D7 7C                  STB   <HEAP   
F19F   97 7D                  STA   <HEAP+1   
F1A1   AF C4                  STX   ,U   
F1A3   39                     RTS      
F1A4                             ; ---- machine code: the grave -----------------------------------------------
F1A4                             ; "`" plus a hex digit loads bytes: ( addr -- addr' ). Pairs of hex digits
F1A4                             ; are stored from addr until a non-hex character; then a RTS (39h) is
F1A4                             ; written and its address is left. An odd last digit is consumed and dropped.
F1A4                             ; "`" plus anything else calls the machine code at TOS: ( addr -- ). The
F1A4                             ; code is entered by JSR (the dispatcher's own), with the address already
F1A4                             ; popped: U points at the top data cell (big-endian, 2 bytes, stack grows
F1A4                             ; down) and the return address is on top of S. The code may pop and push
F1A4                             ; data cells by changing U; on return the cell at ,U is the new TOS. It must
F1A4                             ; keep Y (the interpreter's reading position), DP and S (balanced), and
F1A4                             ; return with RTS. A, B, X, CC may change.
F1A4                             ; Neither the loader's stores nor the code are checked, in either build.
F1A4   8D 20        H_GRAVE:   BSR   hexc   ; the digit after the grave, if any
F1A6   24 1A                  BCC   exec   
F1A8   AE C4                  LDX   ,U   
F1AA   C6 10        HX1:      LDB   #16   
F1AC   3D                     MUL      ; B = the digit, moved up to the high half
F1AD   E7 84                  STB   ,X   ; (an odd digit is overwritten by the RTS)
F1AF   8D 15                  BSR   hexc   
F1B1   24 08                  BCC   hx2   ; odd digit: already consumed, dropped
F1B3   AA 84                  ORA   ,X   
F1B5   A7 80                  STA   ,X+   
F1B7   8D 0D                  BSR   hexc   
F1B9   25 EF                  BCS   hx1   
F1BB   86 39        HX2:      LDA   #39h   ; RTS
F1BD   A7 84                  STA   ,X   
F1BF   AF C4                  STX   ,U   
F1C1   39                     RTS      
F1C2   AE C1        EXEC:     LDX   ,U++   
F1C4   6E 84                  JMP   ,X   ; the code's RTS returns to the dispatcher
F1C6                          IF   CHECKED   
F1C6   BD F0 FD     HEXC:     JSR   isdig   
F1C9   25 0A                  BLO   hv1   ; C = 1
F1CB   84 DF                  ANDA   #0DFh   
F1CD   80 11                  SUBA   #11h   
F1CF   81 06                  CMPA   #6   
F1D1   24 04                  BHS   hv9   ; C = 0
F1D3   80 F6                  SUBA   #0F6h   ; + 10, and sets the carry
F1D5   31 21        HV1:      LEAY   1,Y   ; (LEAY leaves the carry alone)
F1D7   39           HV9:      RTS      
F1D8                          ENDIF      
F1D8                             ; ---- where the two ranges meet ---------------------------------------------
F1D8                             ; The first range ends somewhere among the next five handlers, ] \ [ @ ?
F1D8                             ; (they are in falling code order for this): NPG1 follows. Every handler
F1D8                             ; below them must start in the second range, and every one above in the
F1D8                             ; first.
F1D8                             ; "]" returns: pop an address and jump to it. (PULS X,Y: the dispatcher's
F1D8                             ; return address into X, then the saved IP into Y.)
F1D8   35 30        H_RET:    PULS   X,Y   
F1DA   6E 84                  JMP   ,X   
F1DC                             ; "\" ( flag -- ): true skips to the next ")" or "]" at this level; ")"
F1DC                             ; drops the block start, "]" returns. No closer at all ends the program.
F1DC   EC C1        H_BREAK:   LDD   ,U++   
F1DE   27 5D                  BEQ   sk9   ; false: nothing to do
F1E0   8D 3C                  BSR   skip   
F1E2   4D                     TSTA      ; skip returns 0 for ")"
F1E3                          IF   CHECKED   
F1E3   10 2B FE 5B            LBMI   fin   ; (and FFh for the NUL: the program ends)
F1E7                          ENDIF      
F1E7   26 EF                  BNE   h_ret   
F1E9   35 16        RDROP:    PULS   D,X   ; the return address and the block start
F1EB   1F 05                  TFR   D,PC   ; back to the dispatcher
F1ED                             ; "[" followed by a letter stores the body"s address in that letter"s cell:
F1ED                             ; uppercase is a word, lowercase a variable. Followed by a space it pushes
F1ED                             ; the body"s address instead. Either way it then skips to the matching "]'.
F1ED                             ; (The unchecked build takes anything that is not a letter as the space; the
F1ED                             ; checked build stops on it.)
F1ED                          IF   CHECKED   
F1ED   81 DF        DEF1:     CMPA   #" "-"A"+256   
F1EF   27 1E                  BEQ   def2   
F1F1   31 3F                  LEAY   -1,Y   ; anything but a letter or a space: W. The
F1F3   10 9F 36               STY   <AT   ;   place is that character, just read
F1F6   16 01 61               LBRA   e_brack   
F1F9                          ENDIF      
F1F9   A6 A0        H_DEF:    LDA   ,Y+   
F1FB   80 41                  SUBA   #"A"   ; a letter gives 0-25 or 32-57: lowercase
F1FD   1F 89                  TFR   A,B   ;   lands 64 bytes up
F1FF   C4 DF                  ANDB   #0DFh   ; fold case
F201   C1 1A                  CMPB   #26   
F203                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                              BHS   def2   ; not a letter
F203                          ENDIF      
F203                          IF   CHECKED   
F203   24 E8                  BHS   def1   
F205                          ENDIF      
F205   BD F0 F6               JSR   cellx   
F208   1F 20                  TFR   Y,D   
F20A   E7 84                  STB   ,X   ; little-endian
F20C   A7 01                  STA   1,X   
F20E   8C                     FCB   8Ch   ; (CMPX #: steps over the PSHU)
F20F   36 20        DEF2:     PSHU   Y   ; an anonymous block: push its address
F211                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                                 ; fall into skip
F211                          ENDIF      
F211                          IF   CHECKED   
F211                             ; Checked: the skip must end at a "]" (A = 2), or for a false "(",
F211                             ; which comes to opf, at a ")" (A = 0). Anything else stops with N.
F211   8D 0B                  BSR   skip   
F213   80 02                  SUBA   #2   
F215   8C                     FCB   8Ch   ; (CMPX #: steps over the BSR)
F216   8D 06        OPF:      BSR   skip   
F218   4D                     TSTA      
F219   10 26 01 49            LBNE   e_nest   
F21D   39                     RTS      
F21E                          ENDIF      
F21E                             ; skip: read past text to the closer at this level, and return A = 0 if it
F21E                             ; was ")" and 2 if it was "]". Brackets of both kinds count together;
F21E                             ; strings are stepped over whole. B counts the open levels.
F21E                             ; Unchecked: a NUL first ends the program (for "\" with no closer; anything
F21E                             ; else that runs into the NUL had unbalanced brackets anyway).
F21E                             ; Checked: a NUL, or a string that runs into it, returns A = FFh, and the
F21E                             ; caller decides: "\" ends the program, "(" and "[" stop with N, as they do
F21E                             ; for a closer of the other kind. The place is the opener, still in AT.
F21E   5F           SKIP:     CLRB      
F21F   A6 A0        SK1:      LDA   ,Y+   
F221                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                              LBEQ   fin   
F221                          ENDIF      
F221                          IF   CHECKED   
F221   27 38                  BEQ   ssn   ; A = FFh
F223                          ENDIF      
F223   81 22                  CMPA   #22h   
F225   26 04                  BNE   sk2   
F227   8D 25                  BSR   skipstr   ; leaves A = 22h, which matches nothing below
F229                          IF   CHECKED   
F229   25 12                  BCS   sk9   ; (or FFh, with the carry set: unclosed)
F22B                          ENDIF      
F22B   80 28        SK2:      SUBA   #"("   
F22D   27 0F                  BEQ   sk3   
F22F   4A                     DECA      ; ")"
F230   27 08                  BEQ   sk4   
F232   80 32                  SUBA   #"["-")"   
F234   27 08                  BEQ   sk3   
F236   81 02                  CMPA   #"]"-"["   
F238   26 E5                  BNE   sk1   
F23A   5A           SK4:      DECB      
F23B   2A E2                  BPL   sk1   
F23D   39           SK9:      RTS      ; the closer at this level
F23E   5C           SK3:      INCB      
F23F   20 DE                  BRA   sk1   
F241                             ; 22h, checked build (the unchecked one is with the handlers below).
F241                             ; Checked: a NUL ends the string too, even right after a "/"; skipstr then
F241                             ; returns A = FFh with the carry set (the carry is clear at the quote), and
F241                             ; """ stops with Q, the string's address already pushed. (skip comes here
F241                             ; for its own NUL as well.)
F241                          IF   CHECKED   
F241   36 20        H_STR:    PSHU   Y   
F243   8D 09                  BSR   skipstr   
F245   10 25 01 1A            LBCS   e_quote   
F249   39                     RTS      
F24A   A6 A0        SS0:      LDA   ,Y+   ; the character after the "/"
F24C   27 0D                  BEQ   ssn   
F24E   A6 A0        SKIPSTR:   LDA   ,Y+   
F250   27 09                  BEQ   ssn   
F252   81 2F                  CMPA   #"/"   
F254   27 F4                  BEQ   ss0   
F256   81 22                  CMPA   #22h   
F258   26 F4                  BNE   skipstr   
F25A   39                     RTS      ; the quote: C = 0
F25B   80 01        SSN:      SUBA   #1   ; the NUL: A = FFh, C = 1
F25D   39                     RTS      
F25E                          ENDIF      
F25E   AE C4        H_FETCH:   LDX   ,U   ; "@" (the cell in memory is little-endian)
F260   A6 01                  LDA   1,X   
F262   20 5D                  BRA   cf1   
F264                             ; "?" ( n -- c ) or ( -n -- addr )
F264                             ;   n > 0: wait about n ms for a key; 0 if none came
F264                             ;   n = 0: wait for a key
F264                             ;   n < 0: read a line of at most -n characters, with echo. The buffer
F264                             ;          holds 127 characters and the CR: a bigger count is taken as 127.
F264   AE C4        H_KEY:    LDX   ,U   
F266   2B 17                  BMI   line   
F268   C6 14        KT1:      LDB   #MSLOOP   ; one millisecond, roughly
F26A   BD F0 0D     KT2:      JSR   getk   
F26D   26 0B                  BNE   kt3   
F26F   5A                     DECB      
F270   26 F8                  BNE   kt2   
F272   30 1F                  LEAX   -1,X   
F274   26 F2                  BNE   kt1   ; A = 0 if the time ran out
F276   AE C4                  LDX   ,U   ; 0?: the countdown from 0 took 65536 ms;
F278   27 EE                  BEQ   kt1   ;   run it again, until a key comes
F27A   6F C4        KT3:      CLR   ,U   
F27C   A7 41                  STA   1,U   
F27E   39                     RTS      
F27F                             ; Backspace takes the last character back (and is echoed as it is), CR ends
F27F                             ; (stored, not echoed), every other key is stored and echoed until the line
F27F                             ; is full. B = the length so far; the low byte of the top cell becomes the
F27F                             ; most allowed (it holds minus the count on entry).
F27F   8C FF 81     LINE:     CMPX   #-127   ; (X = TOS, minus the count)
F282   24 04                  BHS   ln1   
F284   86 81                  LDA   #-127   ; more than 127 is taken as 127
F286   A7 41                  STA   1,U   
F288   60 41        LN1:      NEG   1,U   
F28A   8E 82 80               LDX   #LINEBUF   
F28D   5F                     CLRB      
F28E   BD F0 0D     LN2:      JSR   getk   
F291   27 FB                  BEQ   ln2   
F293   81 0D                  CMPA   #13   
F295   27 16                  BEQ   ln5   
F297   81 08                  CMPA   #8   
F299   27 0C                  BEQ   ln4   
F29B   E1 41                  CMPB   1,U   
F29D   24 EF                  BHS   ln2   ; full
F29F   A7 85                  STA   B,X   
F2A1   5C                     INCB      
F2A2   BD FF 03     LN3:      JSR   CONOUT   
F2A5   20 E7                  BRA   ln2   
F2A7   5D           LN4:      TSTB      ; Backspace: nothing to take back?
F2A8   27 E4                  BEQ   ln2   
F2AA   5A                     DECB      
F2AB   20 F5                  BRA   ln3   ; echo it
F2AD   A7 85        LN5:      STA   B,X   ; A = 13
F2AF   AF C4                  STX   ,U   
F2B1   39                     RTS      
F2B2                             ; =============================================================================
F2B2                             ;  Handlers that must start in the second range (unchecked build).
F2B2                             ; =============================================================================
F2B2                             ; "(" ( flag -- ): true pushes the block start and enters; false skips to
F2B2                             ; the matching ")".
F2B2   EC C1        H_OPEN:   LDD   ,U++   
F2B4                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                              BEQ   skip   ; tail call: skip ends in RTS
F2B4                          ENDIF      
F2B4                          IF   CHECKED   
F2B4   10 27 FF 5E            LBEQ   opf   ; checked: skip, and check the closer
F2B8                          ENDIF      
F2B8   35 10                  PULS   X   
F2BA   34 20                  PSHS   Y   
F2BC   6E 84                  JMP   ,X   
F2BE                             ; 22h pushes the address of the text after it and skips the string.
F2BE                             ; skipstr: IP is inside a string; step past its closing quote. "/" escapes
F2BE                             ; the next character, so "/"" does not end it. Leaves A = 22h. (The checked
F2BE                             ; build's is after skip.)
F2BE                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                    H_STR:    PSHU   Y   
                              FCB   8Ch   ; (CMPX #: steps over the LEAY)
                    SS0:      LEAY   1,Y   
                    SKIPSTR:   LDA   ,Y+   
                              CMPA   #"/"   
                              BEQ   ss0   
                              CMPA   #22h   
                              BNE   skipstr   
                              RTS      
F2BE                          ENDIF      
F2BE   AE C4        H_CFETCH:   LDX   ,U   ; ","
F2C0   4F                     CLRA      
F2C1   E6 84        CF1:      LDB   ,X   
F2C3   ED C4                  STD   ,U   
F2C5   39                     RTS      
F2C6                             ; ")" ( flag -- ): true jumps back to the block start (and keeps it); false
F2C6                             ; drops it and carries on.
F2C6   EC C1        H_CLOSE:   LDD   ,U++   
F2C8   10 27 FF 1D            LBEQ   rdrop   
F2CC   10 AE 62               LDY   2,S   ; the block start, under the return address
F2CF   7E F0 00               JMP   pollk   ; the break check, at every loop-back
F2D2                             ; ---- arithmetic and logic: ( NOS TOS -- result ) ---------------------------
F2D2                             ; "*": three 8x8 multiplies; only the low 16 bits are kept.
F2D2                             ; a = ah:al at 2,U.  b = bh:bl at ,U.
F2D2   A6 43        H_MUL:    LDA   3,U   
F2D4   E6 C4                  LDB   ,U   
F2D6   3D                     MUL      ; al*bh
F2D7   E7 C4                  STB   ,U   ; (bh is no longer needed)
F2D9   A6 42                  LDA   2,U   
F2DB   E6 41                  LDB   1,U   
F2DD   3D                     MUL      ; ah*bl
F2DE   EB C4                  ADDB   ,U   
F2E0   E7 C4                  STB   ,U   ; the cross terms, low byte
F2E2   A6 43                  LDA   3,U   
F2E4   E6 41                  LDB   1,U   
F2E6   3D                     MUL      ; al*bl
F2E7   AB C4                  ADDA   ,U   
F2E9   33 42                  LEAU   2,U   
F2EB   ED C4                  STD   ,U   
F2ED   39                     RTS      
F2EE                             ; Signed compares: a-b, then a branch to put -1 or 0 on the stack.
F2EE   8D 18        H_GT:     BSR   h_swap   ; a > b is b < a
F2F0   8D 10        H_LT:     BSR   cmp   
F2F2   2D 02                  BLT   true   
F2F4   5F           FALSE:    CLRB      
F2F5   8C                     FCB   8Ch   ; (CMPX #: steps over the LDB)
F2F6   C6 FF        TRUE:     LDB   #0FFh   
F2F8   1D                     SEX      ; D = 0000 or FFFF
F2F9   ED C4                  STD   ,U   
F2FB   39                     RTS      
F2FC   8D 04        H_EQ:     BSR   cmp   
F2FE   27 F6                  BEQ   true   
F300   20 F2                  BRA   false   
F302   EC 42        CMP:      LDD   2,U   
F304   10 A3 C1               CMPD   ,U++   
F307   39                     RTS      
F308                             ; ---- stack, and printing ----------------------------------------------------
F308   37 16        H_SWAP:   PULU   D,X   ; "%"
F30A   36 06                  PSHU   D   
F30C   36 10                  PSHU   X   
F30E   39                     RTS      
F30F   EC C4        H_DUP:    LDD   ,U   ; ":"
F311   36 06                  PSHU   D   
F313   39                     RTS      
F314   A6 41        H_EMIT:   LDA   1,U   ; "'"
F316                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                              BSR   putc   
F316                          ENDIF      
F316                          IF   CHECKED   
F316   BD FF 03               JSR   CONOUT   ; (the checked build's report is in the way)
F319                          ENDIF      
F319   33 42        H_DROP:   LEAU   2,U   ; ";"
F31B   39                     RTS      
F31C                             ; "$" prints the string at TOS, decoding escapes: "/" plus a character
F31C                             ; clears that character"s bit 6 (/M is CR, /` is space; "/" and ""' have no
F31C                             ; bit 6, so // and /" give themselves).
F31C                             ; Checked: a NUL (not one escaped by "/") stops with Q, the string's address
F31C                             ; still on the stack.
F31C   AE C4        H_PRINT:   LDX   ,U   
F31E   A6 80        PR0:      LDA   ,X+   
F320                          IF   CHECKED   
F320   10 27 00 3F            LBEQ   e_quote   
F324                          ENDIF      
F324   81 22                  CMPA   #22h   
F326   27 F1                  BEQ   h_drop   
F328   81 2F                  CMPA   #"/"   
F32A   26 04                  BNE   pr1   
F32C   A6 80                  LDA   ,X+   
F32E   84 BF                  ANDA   #0BFh   
F330                PR1:         
F330                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                              BSR   putc   
F330                          ENDIF      
F330                          IF   CHECKED   
F330   BD FF 03               JSR   CONOUT   
F333                          ENDIF      
F333   20 E9                  BRA   pr0   
F335                             ; "!" ( n addr -- ) is "." with the high byte stored first. The cell in
F335                             ; memory is little-endian.
F335                             ; Checked: both bytes must be in the program's space, and they are tested
F335                             ; before either is stored (chkst stops with O, the stack untouched).
F335   AE C4        H_STORE:   LDX   ,U   
F337                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                              LDA   2,U   
                              STA   1,X   
F337                          ENDIF      
F337                          IF   CHECKED   
F337   8D 13                  BSR   chkst   
F339   30 01                  LEAX   1,X   
F33B   8D 0F                  BSR   chkst   
F33D   A6 42                  LDA   2,U   
F33F   A7 84                  STA   ,X   
F341                             ; and fall into ".", which loads X again (and checks it again)
F341                          ENDIF      
F341                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                              FCB   8Ch   ; (CMPX #: steps over the LDX)
F341                          ENDIF      
F341   AE C4        H_CSTORE:   LDX   ,U   ; "." ( c addr -- )
F343                          IF   CHECKED   
F343   8D 07                  BSR   chkst   
F345                          ENDIF      
F345   33 42                  LEAU   2,U   
F347   37 06                  PULU   D   
F349   E7 84                  STB   ,X   
F34B   39                     RTS      
F34C                          IF   CHECKED   
F34C                             ; ---- reached from a handler ------------------------------------------------
F34C                             ; chkst: stop with O unless X is in the program's own space: from the letter
F34C                             ; page up to HEAPLIM, so the interpreter's stacks and whatever lies above the
F34C                             ; limit are safe. Memory above the heap top but below the limit is the
F34C                             ; program's own: Tiny BASIC keeps its lines there. Keeps every register.
F34C   8C 82 00     CHKST:    CMPX   #LET   
F34F   25 06                  BLO   cs9   
F351   8C F0 00               CMPX   #HEAPLIM*256   
F354   24 01                  BHS   cs9   
F356   39                     RTS      ; in range
F357   86 4F        CS9:      LDA   #"O"   
F359   8C                     FCB   8Ch   
F35A   86 57        E_BRACK:   LDA   #"W"   ; [ and a bad character (AT is set)
F35C   8C                     FCB   8Ch   
F35D   86 5A        E_ZERO:   LDA   #"Z"   ; / by zero
F35F   8C                     FCB   8Ch   
F360   86 48        E_HEAP:   LDA   #"H"   ; _ past the limit, or below the program's end
F362   8C                     FCB   8Ch   
F363   86 51        E_QUOTE:   LDA   #"Q"   ; " or $ ran into the NUL
F365   8C                     FCB   8Ch   
F366   86 4E        E_NEST:   LDA   #"N"   ; a skip from ( or [: the NUL or the wrong closer
F368                             ; and fall into error
F368                             ; =============================================================================
F368                             ;  Checked build: the error report. A = the letter, AT = the place; U is
F368                             ;  as the program left it, and SSAV holds S as the failing character began
F368                             ;  (see "the error entries" after `upper`).
F368                             ;  It sits here, ahead of h_num, pdec and putc, so that it reaches them with
F368                             ;  short calls. Prints
F368                             ; 
F368                             ;     CR LF
F368                             ;     Err X @ line,col CR LF
F368                             ;     <up to 16 raw characters from the place, ending early at CR, LF, NUL>
F368                             ;     CR LF
F368                             ;     Stk n:[ ...][ v]*  CR LF     (the top 8 cells, bottom to top, signed)
F368                             ;     Rtn n CR LF
F368                             ; 
F368                             ;  and goes to EXIT. Line and column count from 1: the line is one more
F368                             ;  than the LFs between PROG and the place, the column the distance from the
F368                             ;  last LF (or from PROG-1). A place below PROG is in the -n? line buffer:
F368                             ;  line 0, column = its offset there + 1. Numbers other than the cells are
F368                             ;  printed unsigned (pdec), the cells signed (h_num).
F368                             ; 
F368                             ;  The data stack may be one cell past its limit (S, U = 80FEh): the
F368                             ;  report's own cells then reach 8 bytes further down, to 80F6h, into the
F368                             ;  return stack page, so the report runs on a fresh return stack at RSREP
F368                             ;  (80F0h), below those bytes.
F368                             ; =============================================================================
F368   1F 89        ERROR:    TFR   A,B   ; the letter (pmsg and CONOUT keep B)
F36A   BD F4 2A               JSR   pmsg   
F36D   0D 0A 45 72 72 A0      FCB   13,10,"Err"," "+80h   
F373   1F 98                  TFR   B,A   
F375   BD FF 03               JSR   CONOUT   
F378   CC 81 00               LDD   #RSTOP   ; the return stack's depth, (RSTOP - S) / 2,
F37B   93 3A                  SUBD   <SSAV   ;   S as it was when this character began
F37D   44                     LSRA      
F37E   56                     RORB      
F37F   10 CE 80 F0            LDS   #RSREP   
F383   36 06                  PSHU   D   ; kept on the data stack, printed last
F385   BD F4 2A               JSR   pmsg   
F388   20 40 A0               FCB   " @"," "+80h   
F38B                             ; the place: Y counts the lines, X walks, the cell at ,U holds the
F38B                             ; address of the last LF (PROG-1 to begin with)
F38B   10 8E 00 00            LDY   #0   
F38F   8E 82 7F               LDX   #LINEBUF-1   
F392   36 10                  PSHU   X   
F394   8E 82 FF               LDX   #PROG-1   
F397   9C 36                  CMPX   <AT   
F399   24 14                  BHS   lc3   ; the place is below PROG: line 0
F39B   AF C4                  STX   ,U   
F39D   31 21        LC1:      LEAY   1,Y   ; a line
F39F   30 01        LC2:      LEAX   1,X   
F3A1   9C 36                  CMPX   <AT   
F3A3   24 0A                  BHS   lc3   
F3A5   A6 84                  LDA   ,X   
F3A7   81 0A                  CMPA   #10   
F3A9   26 F4                  BNE   lc2   
F3AB   AF C4                  STX   ,U   
F3AD   20 EE                  BRA   lc1   
F3AF   DC 36        LC3:      LDD   <AT   
F3B1   A3 C4                  SUBD   ,U   
F3B3   ED C4                  STD   ,U   ; the column
F3B5   36 20                  PSHU   Y   
F3B7   BD F4 42               JSR   pdec   ; the line
F3BA   8D 6E                  BSR   pmsg   
F3BC   AC                     FCB   ","+80h   
F3BD   BD F4 42               JSR   pdec   ; the column
F3C0   8D 68                  BSR   pmsg   
F3C2   0D 8A                  FCB   13,10+80h   
F3C4                             ; the text at the place
F3C4   9E 36                  LDX   <AT   
F3C6   C6 10                  LDB   #16   
F3C8   A6 80        TX1:      LDA   ,X+   
F3CA   27 0E                  BEQ   tx9   
F3CC   81 0A                  CMPA   #10   
F3CE   27 0A                  BEQ   tx9   
F3D0   81 0D                  CMPA   #13   
F3D2   27 06                  BEQ   tx9   
F3D4   BD F4 5B               JSR   putc   
F3D7   5A                     DECB      
F3D8   26 EE                  BNE   tx1   
F3DA   8D 4E        TX9:      BSR   pmsg   
F3DC   0D 0A 53 74 6B A0      FCB   13,10,"Stk"," "+80h   
F3E2                             ; the data stack: its depth, then its top 8 cells, from Y down to
F3E2                             ; the program"s top cell, which is under the return stack"s depth,
F3E2                             ; at 2,U.
F3E2   31 42                  LEAY   2,U   
F3E4   34 20                  PSHS   Y   ; where the walk ends
F3E6   CC 81 FC               LDD   #DSTOP   
F3E9   A3 E4                  SUBD   ,S   
F3EB   44                     LSRA      
F3EC   56                     RORB      
F3ED   36 06                  PSHU   D   
F3EF   8D 51                  BSR   pdec   ; the depth
F3F1   8D 37                  BSR   pmsg   
F3F3   BA                     FCB   ":"+80h   
F3F4   31 A8 10               LEAY   16,Y   ; past the 8th cell from the top ...
F3F7   10 8C 81 FC            CMPY   #DSTOP   
F3FB   24 08                  BHS   sl1   
F3FD   8D 2B                  BSR   pmsg   ; (there are more than 8)
F3FF   20 2E 2E AE            FCB   " ..","."+80h   
F403   20 04                  BRA   sl2   
F405   10 8E 81 FC  SL1:      LDY   #DSTOP   ; ... or the whole stack, if no more than 8
F409   10 AC E4     SL2:      CMPY   ,S   
F40C   23 0B                  BLS   sl9   
F40E   EC A3                  LDD   ,--Y   
F410   36 06                  PSHU   D   
F412   8D 16                  BSR   pmsg   
F414   A0                     FCB   " "+80h   
F415   8D 21                  BSR   h_num   
F417   20 F0                  BRA   sl2   
F419   8D 0F        SL9:      BSR   pmsg   
F41B   0D 0A 52 74 6E A0      FCB   13,10,"Rtn"," "+80h   
F421   8D 1F                  BSR   pdec   ; the depth of the return stack, pushed first
F423   8D 05                  BSR   pmsg   
F425   0D 8A                  FCB   13,10+80h   
F427   7E FF 09               JMP   EXIT   
F42A                             ; pmsg: print the text after the call, up to and including the character
F42A                             ; that has bit 7 set (it is printed without it), then return after it.
F42A   35 10        PMSG:     PULS   X   
F42C   A6 84        PM1:      LDA   ,X   
F42E   84 7F                  ANDA   #7Fh   
F430   8D 29                  BSR   putc   
F432   6D 80                  TST   ,X+   
F434   2A F6                  BPL   pm1   
F436   6E 84                  JMP   ,X   
F438                          ENDIF      
F438                             ; "#" prints TOS as a signed decimal number, with no space after it.
F438   6D C4        H_NUM:    TST   ,U   
F43A   2A 06                  BPL   pdec   
F43C   86 2D                  LDA   #"-"   
F43E   8D 1B                  BSR   putc   
F440   8D 5F                  BSR   negt   
F442                             ; pdec: print the top cell as unsigned and drop it, by recursion on /10
F442   CC 00 0A     PDEC:     LDD   #10   
F445   36 06                  PSHU   D   
F447   8D 69                  BSR   udiv   ; NOS = quotient, TOS = digit
F449   37 06                  PULU   D   ; the digit
F44B   34 04                  PSHS   B   
F44D   EC C4                  LDD   ,U   
F44F   27 04                  BEQ   pd1   
F451   8D EF                  BSR   pdec   
F453   20 02                  BRA   pd2   
F455   33 42        PD1:      LEAU   2,U   ; drop the zero quotient
F457   35 02        PD2:      PULS   A   
F459   8B 30                  ADDA   #"0"   ; and fall into putc
F45B   7E FF 03     PUTC:     JMP   CONOUT   
F45E                             ; ---- more arithmetic ---------------------------------------------------------
F45E   EC C1        H_AND:    LDD   ,U++   
F460   A4 C4                  ANDA   ,U   
F462   E4 41                  ANDB   1,U   
F464   20 04                  BRA   st   
F466   EC C1        H_ADD:    LDD   ,U++   
F468   E3 C4                  ADDD   ,U   
F46A   ED C4        ST:       STD   ,U   
F46C   39                     RTS      
F46D                             ; "-" has two jobs: directly before a digit it starts a negative number.
F46D   BD F0 FD     H_SUB:    JSR   isdig   
F470   25 2C                  BLO   negnum   
F472   EC 42                  LDD   2,U   
F474   A3 C1                  SUBD   ,U++   
F476   20 F2                  BRA   st   
F478                             ; ---- the tail ---------------------------------------------------------------
F478                             ; "/" is the last handler, so what follows its first byte may lie past the
F478                             ; second range: the divide itself and the routines after it.
F478                             ; "/" ( a b -- q r ): the remainder is on top. Truncates toward zero; r takes
F478                             ; a's sign. Divide |a| by |b|, then q gets the sign of a XOR b and r the sign
F478                             ; of a. Unchecked, dividing by zero returns two cells of no meaning; checked,
F478                             ; it stops with Z, both operands still on the stack.
F478                H_DIV:       
F478                          IF   CHECKED   
F478   EC C4                  LDD   ,U   
F47A   10 27 FE DF            LBEQ   e_zero   
F47E                          ENDIF      
F47E   A6 42                  LDA   2,U   
F480   34 02                  PSHS   A   ; a's sign: for r
F482   A8 C4                  EORA   ,U   
F484   34 02                  PSHS   A   ; a xor b: for q
F486   30 42                  LEAX   2,U   
F488   8D 22                  BSR   absx   ; |a|
F48A   1F 31                  TFR   U,X   
F48C   8D 1E                  BSR   absx   ; |b|
F48E   8D 22                  BSR   udiv   ; NOS = q, TOS = r
F490   30 42                  LEAX   2,U   
F492   6D E0                  TST   ,S+   
F494   2A 02                  BPL   dv1   
F496   8D 0B                  BSR   negx   ; q's sign
F498   6D E0        DV1:      TST   ,S+   
F49A   2A 0F                  BPL   ng9   
F49C   20 03                  BRA   negt   ; r's sign
F49E   BD F1 04     NEGNUM:   JSR   rdnum   ; a negative literal: read it, then negate
F4A1   1F 31        NEGT:     TFR   U,X   
F4A3   EC 84        NEGX:     LDD   ,X   ; negx: negate the cell at X
F4A5   40                     NEGA      
F4A6   50                     NEGB      
F4A7   82 00                  SBCA   #0   
F4A9   ED 84                  STD   ,X   
F4AB   39           NG9:      RTS      
F4AC   6D 84        ABSX:     TST   ,X   ; absx: negate the cell at X if negative
F4AE   2A FB                  BPL   ng9   
F4B0   20 F1                  BRA   negx   
F4B2                             ; udiv: unsigned divide, in place. The dividend is the NOS cell and the
F4B2                             ; divisor the TOS cell, both <= 8000h; the NOS cell becomes the quotient and
F4B2                             ; the TOS cell the remainder. The remainder is built in D (always < the
F4B2                             ; divisor, so 2R+1 fits in 16 bits).
F4B2                             ; Dividing by 2 is one shift (the spec wants that fast).
F4B2   EC C4        UDIV:     LDD   ,U   
F4B4   83 00 02               SUBD   #2   
F4B7   26 07                  BNE   ud0   
F4B9   64 42                  LSR   2,U   
F4BB   66 43                  ROR   3,U   ; the quotient
F4BD   59                     ROLB      ; the remainder: the bit that fell out (D was 0)
F4BE   20 18                  BRA   ud3   
F4C0   8E 00 10     UD0:      LDX   #16   
F4C3   4F                     CLRA      
F4C4   5F                     CLRB      
F4C5   68 43        UD1:      ASL   3,U   
F4C7   69 42                  ROL   2,U   ; the dividend's top bit ...
F4C9   59                     ROLB      
F4CA   49                     ROLA      ; ... into the remainder
F4CB   10 A3 C4               CMPD   ,U   
F4CE   25 04                  BLO   ud2   
F4D0   A3 C4                  SUBD   ,U   
F4D2   6C 43                  INC   3,U   ; a quotient bit
F4D4   30 1F        UD2:      LEAX   -1,X   
F4D6   26 ED                  BNE   ud1   
F4D8   ED C4        UD3:      STD   ,U   
F4DA   39                     RTS      
F4DB                IMGEND:      


